# Public copy & i18n (EN + FR)

Companion to [`comms-public-ux.mdc`](comms-public-ux.mdc) (product language lock, copy
style) and [`seo.mdc`](seo.mdc) (canonicals, sitemap). Written after the
2026-08-11 QOL pass, which found that the catalog looked healthy at the lead line
while French carried real meaning errors underneath. Findings and before/after:
[`docs/audit/public-copy-qol-2026-08.md`](../../docs/audit/public-copy-qol-2026-08.md);
lessons: [`docs/audit/session-knowledge-2026-08-11-public-copy-qol.md`](../../docs/audit/session-knowledge-2026-08-11-public-copy-qol.md).

## The rule that matters most

**French is not a mirror of English — it is a second source of truth that can be
wrong.** Key parity passing tells you nothing about whether the two locales say
the same thing. The worst bug found in the QOL pass was `photoConsentGuide`
telling stewards in French to prefer group photos *"sans consentement individuel"*
(without individual consent) — the exact opposite of the English. It had passed
every existing check for months.

When you touch a French string, read the English one beside it and confirm the
**claim** matches, not just the topic. When you touch an English string, update
the French value in the same commit.

## Mechanical guards (run these, do not hand-audit)

| Check | Lives in |
|---|---|
| Sentence starts capitalized (EN + FR) | [`public-copy-style.test.ts`](../../src/lib/comms/public-copy-style.test.ts) |
| No bare "the hub" in EN public copy | same |
| One French name per locked term | same |
| French space before `:` and `;` | same |
| No developer jargon | same |
| No untranslated FR (identical to EN, >4 words) | same |
| Named lead-length limits + ≤1 em dash on leads | same |
| SEO description length band, duplicates, capitalization | [`public-page-meta.test.ts`](../../src/lib/seo/public-page-meta.test.ts) |
| Smoke-asserted EN prose still in `messages/en.json` (COPY-002) | [`smoke-asserted-copy.test.ts`](../../src/lib/comms/smoke-asserted-copy.test.ts) |

```bash
npm run test:unit -- src/lib/comms/public-copy-style.test.ts src/lib/seo/public-page-meta.test.ts src/lib/comms/smoke-asserted-copy.test.ts
```

Failures print the offending key path and value. **Fix the copy, not the guard** —
if a check is genuinely wrong, change it deliberately and say why in the commit,
the way the blanket word ceiling was removed on 2026-08-11.

**Adding a check? Verify it by injecting the regression it claims to catch.** A
guard you have not tried to break is a guess. Doing this on 2026-08-11 is what
revealed that `nav` — which holds the locked tool names — was missing from
`PUBLIC_NS` and had never been scanned. Throwaway harness:
[`session-knowledge-2026-08-11-public-copy-qol.md`](../../docs/audit/session-knowledge-2026-08-11-public-copy-qol.md)
(lesson 2).

## Locked terms and their French names

Never rename these, and never let French invent a second name:

| English (locked) | French (locked) |
|---|---|
| Officer Hub (only for `/app`) | Hub des dirigeants |
| Brand Kit | Trousse de marque (capitalized — it is a product name) |
| UnionOps Comms / "this site" | UnionOps Comms / « ce site » |
| Flyer Maker → a *flyer* | Créateur de tracts → un **tract** (not *affiche* = poster, not *dépliant* = leaflet) |
| alt text | texte **alternatif** (never the clipped "texte alt") |
| Duty of Fair Representation / DFR | devoir de représentation équitable / **DRE** |
| OHSA | **LSST** |
| ESA | **LNE** |

*Poster* is `affiche`, so `affiche` is correct for Solidarity Posters and QR Board
Posters — the flyer rule is specifically about Flyer Maker output.

## Plain language for volunteers

The audience is Ontario public-sector and college-sector stewards, LEC officers,
and workshop volunteers. Not marketers, developers, or lawyers.

Banned on public strings (the guard enforces these): `tenant`, `canvas/install/brand
chrome`, `type scale`, `progressive web app`, `PCI`, `slug`, `memory store`,
`localStorage`, `CTA`, `utilize`, `leverage`, `*_DB_BACKEND`.

Say the thing instead: "starter values from published union graphics guidelines",
"text size", "your browser's own app-install feature", "share link name",
"call to action".

**One documented exception:** `privacyPage.hubSelfHost` keeps `AUTH_SECRET`,
because that paragraph addresses whoever self-hosts the Officer Hub, not stewards.
It is exempted by key path in the guard. Add exceptions the same way — by key,
with a comment — rather than by weakening a pattern.

## French typography and idiom

- A space goes before `:` and `;` (`Un message : quatre canaux`). Guarded.
- Prefer `p. ex.` over `e.g.`, and `…` over `...`.
- Watch for calques that invert or change meaning: *"Vérifiez **contre** votre
  convention"* → `dans`; *"moved camp"* → not `changé de camp` (that reads as
  switching sides); *"paywalls"* → `murs payants`; *"votre central"* → name it
  (`votre syndicat provincial ou national`).
- Do not drop the clause that carries the reason. French had lost *"so the board
  never looks abandoned"* and *"so updates do not die when someone leaves"* — the
  sentence still parsed, but the advice no longer explained itself.

## Body copy vs lead copy

There is intentionally **no blanket per-leaf word ceiling** (removed 2026-08-11 —
it rewarded clipping subjects and verbs). Guide paragraphs, tips, checklist items,
and hints must read as complete sentences a steward could say aloud. Only a few
*named* lead fields stay short, and lead fields cap at one em dash.

Error, empty, and success states owe the reader **a consequence and a remedy**.
"Invalid brand kit file" names neither; "That file is not a Brand Kit export. Pick
the .json file you downloaded from Brand Kit and try again." names both.

## Editing hazards

- **Mechanical find-and-replace leaves a fingerprint.** An earlier pass swapped
  semicolons and dashes for periods and left ten SEO descriptions starting a
  sentence lowercase, which rendered verbatim in search results. If you run a bulk
  replace, run the guards after and read the diff.
- **Prefer a temp `.mjs` script over a PowerShell one-liner** for bulk catalog
  edits; PowerShell mangles quotes and `$` in JSON strings. Delete the script
  before committing.
- **`JSON.stringify` round-trips are not byte-safe** on these files (line endings
  and trailing newline differ). Do raw-text replaces, or use `StrReplace`.
- Semicolons never appear in JSON syntax, so a raw-text semicolon pass is safe.
  Colons do — never bulk-replace those.
- **Edit values, not keys.** EN/FR key parity is asserted; renaming a key in one
  locale breaks the other.

## Do not

- Reintroduce a blanket word-count ceiling
- Hardcode a national union name, colour, or hashtag into generic copy (OPSEU/CAAT
  is reference tenant #1, not a default) — prefer `#LocalUnion` + `[Local Number]`
- Leak env vars, cron paths, or `*_DB_BACKEND` into volunteer-facing copy
- Weaken the legal meaning of "not legal advice" / "aid only" disclaimers
- Assume a smoke assertion still matches the catalog — `builders.smoke.spec.ts`
  spent weeks asserting `Local-first Comms` after that string was deleted.
  **COPY-002 closed:** `npm run test:unit -- src/lib/comms/smoke-asserted-copy.test.ts`
  fails if a plain-string public Comms smoke assertion disappears from `messages/en.json`.
  Prefer regex (`/Graphic Maker/i`) or restore catalog copy; allowlist only COMMS_SOURCES
  titles in `smoke-asserted-copy.ts`.
